  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A resistor connects two parallel conducting rails a distance d apart. A conducting bar rolls along the rails at a constant velocity v through a uniform magnetic field of 2.0 T perpendicular to the rails as shown.</p>\n<p>The voltage V across the resistor is measured.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>The graph shows the variation of V with d.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_02\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 2\" src=\"asset:fig_02\"/></figure></p>\n<p>What is v?</p>\n<p>[1]</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">0.33 m s<sup>−1</sup></li><li data-label=\"B\">3.0 m s<sup>−1</sup></li><li data-label=\"C\">6.0 m s<sup>−1</sup></li><li data-label=\"D\">12.0 m s<sup>−1</sup></li></ol>"
  },
